# What the PRO artifact does not carry.
#
# Pro's own, beside Pro's tree, because Pro is a separate plugin rather than a
# build of the same one (ADR 0014) and the two artifacts are staged from two
# different roots. One shared file would have to name paths that exist in only
# one of them, which is how a rule meant for free ends up silently doing
# nothing to Pro.
#
# Short, because pro/ is already almost all shippable code: it has no Composer
# manifest, no node_modules and no build config of its own — Pro's Vite config
# lives at the repo root and is stripped by never being copied.
#
# `resources/` STAYS, as it does for free. Pro is not distributed on wp.org so
# Guideline 4 does not reach it, but Pro's loader source is the honest record
# of what its bundle is, and there is no reason to ship less of it than free
# ships of its own. bin/verify-artifact-contract.sh does not assert it here —
# see the note in that script on why (d) has one direction.

# Tests and analysis
/tests
/phpstan-bootstrap.php

# This file
/.distignore

# Editor and OS litter, at any depth
.DS_Store
